    pr_ref:  # b5d1
    description: "Adjacent finding of audit-findings 0021 (docs/audits/0021-logging-family.md, Step 5). Filed, not moved.\nipc_send is \"data sent to another process over a channel the program set up\" (the audit's definition, now in io_boundary_types and ADR-0050). These rows cross NO process boundary -- an in-process notification is delivered to observers in the same process:\n- objc NSNotificationCenter: postNotificationName:object:, postNotificationName:object:userInfo:, postNotification: (the row's own note: \"In-process pub/sub; classified as IPC for boundary analysis\")\n- swift NotificationCenter.post (\"In-process pub/sub notification posting\")\nTheir cross-process siblings NSDistributedNotificationCenter / DistributedNotificationCenter are correctly ipc_send and are NOT in scope.\nEffect: each post is an `ipc` taint sink and an ipc_send headline crossing. Not measured on a corpus.\nRelated: WI-rivur item 2 (NSNotificationCenter.removeObserver rowed ipc_recv) -- same root (\"a boundary chosen by what the call is ABOUT, not what it DOES\"), different rows.\nFix shape (not decided): delete the rows (no crossing), or a non-crossing representation if one exists. Measure the removal direction: every lost ipc finding must be read back."  # b5d1
    fields: {}  # b5d1
- op: discuss  # b344
  at: '2026-10-03T15:03:55Z'  # b344
  by: agent  # b344
  actor: jgstern_agent  # b344
  clock: 2  # b344
  nonce: b344  # b344
  message: "IMPLEMENTED on branch jgstern-agent/fix/audit0021-rows (local, not pushed), commit a05b58014f. Decision: DELETE (no process boundary crossed; no in-process value exists to move to). objc NSNotificationCenter post* (3) and swift NotificationCenter.post removed; Distributed* centers stay ipc_send (pinned). Taint: four ipc sinks gone; calls now external_potential. Removal direction read back on a corpus A/B: every ipc_send chain lost on AFNetworking (8), ResearchKit (7), SDWebImage (5), CocoaLumberjack (3), Kingfisher (3), swift-composable-architecture (2) was an in-process post (arm B has zero ipc_send chains there); NO-IPC-SEND went violated->inconclusive on all six, never confirmed. ipc taint claims were inconclusive in both arms on those repos, so the taint effect is evidenced by the derivation test only. Report: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_10032026/ragaz.md (OUTCOME, draft CLOSURE NOTE, A/B artifacts in run_10032026/ragaz/). Tests: red then green on the board; branch affected-test run 9955 passed + 8 failed (7 were pins of the old rows, fixed in fdb14eb77e; 1 hypothesis health-check under load), re-run of those files 1138 passed. No status change made."  # b344
